spans.s:
cl. 1. Ā. ˚टते (exceptionally P. ˚ति, MBh. iii, 14703; Vet. ii, 9/10; जघटे, घटिष्यते [Naiṣ.], अघटिष्ट, Bhaṭṭ.),
to be intently occupied about, be busy with, strive or endeavour after, exert one's self for (loc. dat. acc. [MBh. iii, 14703], प्रति, -अर्थम् and अर्थे; inf. Pāṇ. iii, 4, 65; Bhaṭṭ.);
to reach, come to (loc.), Vet. ii, 9/10;
to fall to the share of (loc.), Naiṣ. x, 47;
to take effect, answer, Kathās. cxxiv; Rājat. vi, 361;
to happen, take place, be possible, suit, BhP.; Hcar.; Śiś. ix, 4; Ratnāv.; Naiṣ.; Sarvad. &c.;
to be in connection or united with (instr.), Mālatīm. ii, 8; Daś. viii, 34; Rājat. iv, 617;
 (for √ घट्ट्) to hurt with words, speak of malignantly, Hariv. ii, 1, 31 :
Caus. P. घटयति (Pāṇ. vi, 4, 92; exceptionally Ā. ˚ते, Rājat. iv, 543),
to join together, connect, bring together, unite, Suśr.; Śiś. ix, 87; Naiṣ. i, 46; Ratnāv.;
to shut, Hcar. v, 253 (v.l.);
to put or place or lay on (loc.), Gīt. v, vii, xii;
to bring near, procure, Bhartṛ. iii, 18; Amar.; Kathās. xviii; Vet.;
to effect, accomplish, produce, make, form, fashion, Mṛcch.; VarBṛ.; Pañcat. &c.;
to do a service (acc.) to any one (gen.), Rājat. v, 543;
to impel, Bhaṭṭ. x, 73;
to exert one's self, MBh. iii, 14702;
 (for √ घट्ट्, Caus.) to rub, graze, touch, move, agitate, iv, vi (C), vii, xii (5363, C):
Caus. घाटयति, to hurt, injure, Dhātup. xxxiii, 49;
to unite or put together, ib.;
 ‘to speak’ or ‘to shine’ 93.

; Suśr.; Kāvyād. iii, 110;
to stir round, Suśr. iv, 14, 8;
 to have a bad effect or influence on (acc.), Car. viii, 7, 28;
